WEBVTT

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.120
Oh, sir, something terrible has happened.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.920
We have a guest.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:23.590
What's that?

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:29.920
I'm here.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.120
What happened, sister?

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.740
Too early in the morning for me.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:41.480
I thought this was a hotel.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.200
Hotel?

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.720
Two blocks down the street.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:46.110
Hey, wait a minute.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.370
It's a hotel.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:50.960
Don't make up your mind.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.480
Have you got a room?

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:53.960
Have we got a room?

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.410
Well, sir, we did have one someplace.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:01:59.830
Oh, wait a minute.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:08.510
How does it look?

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.610
Not so encouraging, sir.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:13.660
Oh, oui!

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.060
You're getting hot.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:16.650
You're telling me.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:17.550
There.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.160
We might let her have that one.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.620
How would you like a laundry?

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.460
Now, just a minute.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.900
I'm not the sort of a person you can monkey with.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.220
But I don't want to monkey.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:35.740
I get what I want and I've handled fresh clerks before.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.760
Now I'm gonna tell you just what you're up against.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.500
Do you know why I'm here?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.980
No, I didn't know why you were here.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.380
Now don't tell me, uh, you're here to get a room.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.480
No, kill a man.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.010
I beg your pardon.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:53.450
Unless he does the right thing

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:54.770
for my kid sister Genevieve.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.300
Oh, that's the way it is with you.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.700
That's the way it is.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.200
Now, do we play some more, or do I get what I want?

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.150
Sister, if I've got what you want, you've got what you want.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.340
Now get that 418, that room there.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:13.920
Get the one with a red carpet.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.200
How do you look on a red carpet?

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:15.740
Make it green.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.520
Make that a green carpet.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.280
Hey, boy, now go ahead, now get the grip there.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.780
Everybody get the grip, boy.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:35.090
Benton handles your plane pretty well, doesn't he, Riemer?

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:37.280
He's the greatest pilot in America.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.750
How about this Robert story that wrote Whatever Goes Up?

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.750
Never saw him fly, but if he flies anything like he writes, he's a wonder.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:45.130
Yeah.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.050
By the way, got a pilot for the race yet, Howard?

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:53.580
Why, I've got a couple coming up from San Diego this weekend to talk it over.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:58.100
Want to increase that bet of ours, say, to 10,000?

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:58.700
Yes!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.160
That's not too bad.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.940
Why, if I get the right kind of pilot, I'll talk to you.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.030
Any time.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:19.840
Lives at White Beach tomorrow.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:20.360
