00:37:14.960 --> 00:37:16.910
I found out about that.

00:37:17.240 --> 00:37:17.500
Good.

00:37:17.640 --> 00:37:18.700
Then that's all you need to know.

00:37:19.010 --> 00:37:23.450
This mechanic is going to bring a pilot over from Glendale who's going to ride in the plane with you as a passenger.

00:37:23.820 --> 00:37:25.240
A weight handicap to Benton.

00:37:25.580 --> 00:37:27.580
That'll give you a chance to tell more lies, see?

00:37:28.060 --> 00:37:28.940
Yes, I see.

00:37:29.600 --> 00:37:29.820
Now.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:31.020
Give me that key.

00:37:31.340 --> 00:37:33.880
The minute the plane's off the ground, the pilot will take it over.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:36.260
See? Perfectly safe.

00:37:36.600 --> 00:37:38.200
And besides, you'll have a parachute.

00:37:39.810 --> 00:37:41.570
Don't mention parachutes.

00:37:42.220 --> 00:37:48.240
Guys, I'm scared to death of those darn things.

00:37:48.400 --> 00:37:51.880
Act like a baby.

00:37:52.140 --> 00:37:53.880
You don't want Peggy to know you're a coward, do you?

00:37:54.430 --> 00:37:55.550
Oh, I don't care.

00:37:55.730 --> 00:37:56.670
Why, of course you care.

00:37:56.920 --> 00:37:59.320
You're crazy about her, and she's crazy about you.

00:37:59.620 --> 00:37:59.960
Well, I...

00:38:00.090 --> 00:38:01.850
I can't do her any good dead, can I?

00:38:01.990 --> 00:38:02.730
Sure you can.

00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:04.200
How?

00:38:04.520 --> 00:38:05.160
The insurance.

00:38:06.180 --> 00:38:06.580
Insurance?

00:38:07.920 --> 00:38:08.800
What insurance?

00:38:09.180 --> 00:38:09.960
Why, it's all fixed.

00:38:10.080 --> 00:38:11.380
We're taking out some insurance.

00:38:11.650 --> 00:38:13.130
The doctors are going to examine you in the morning.

00:38:13.560 --> 00:38:15.700
Well, nobody is going to examine me.

00:38:16.020 --> 00:38:17.940
The rules of the race require an examination.

00:38:18.200 --> 00:38:20.140
I'm just killing two birds with one stone.

00:38:20.950 --> 00:38:24.590
Well, I can't speak for the other bird, but you can count me out.

00:38:24.750 --> 00:38:29.920
I don't think you appreciate how good I am to you.

00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:33.020
Well, I fixed it so that Peggy's going to get half the insurance money.

00:38:34.390 --> 00:38:35.210
Oh, yeah?

00:38:35.820 --> 00:38:37.460
Well, who's going to get the other half?

00:38:38.040 --> 00:38:40.470
Well, I've got to get something out of this.

00:39:19.610 --> 00:39:23.600
Open this door! What's the idea?

00:39:26.740 --> 00:39:27.540
Open the door!

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:54.190
the moon? So you're going to have help. I don't think his mind is on the moon. Oh, is that so?

00:40:01.980 --> 00:40:02.940
That's what I was doing.

00:40:11.840 --> 00:40:13.000
That boy's scared.

00:40:13.350 --> 00:40:15.230
I'll take a bet he's trying to sneak out on us.

00:40:15.710 --> 00:40:18.010
Say, you wouldn't say that to Mr. Story's face.

00:40:18.170 --> 00:40:18.590
That's right.

00:40:19.020 --> 00:40:20.540
Let's hear you say it to my face.

00:40:20.710 --> 00:40:21.810
I said that you were...

00:40:21.810 --> 00:40:22.230
Never mind.

00:40:22.880 --> 00:40:24.500
I said that you were scared to death,

00:40:24.700 --> 00:40:26.160
that you were trying to sneak out of town.

00:40:27.400 --> 00:40:27.780
Ridiculous.

00:40:28.240 --> 00:40:29.980
Why, you don't think I'd be leaving town...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.240
without my luggage, do you?

00:40:36.970 --> 00:40:38.590
Lane is always clowning.

00:40:38.980 --> 00:40:40.140
Cut it out now, Lane.

00:40:40.540 --> 00:40:42.740
I'm afraid Howard will have to get another pilot.

00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:44.360
Good night.

00:40:47.190 --> 00:40:49.770
Isn't it funny what jealousy will lead a man to say?

00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:52.340
There's no any truth in what he said, is there?

00:40:53.190 --> 00:40:53.590
Mademoiselle.

00:40:53.770 --> 00:40:59.920
Be that you'll fly to win.

00:41:00.190 --> 00:41:07.280
all right I'll fly to win but don't be disappointed if you're disappointed but

00:41:07.340 --> 00:41:12.210
you are confident now aren't you mmm so confident that I'm gonna take along a

00:41:12.210 --> 00:41:22.760
passenger just to make Benton look silly what take my first flight with you no no

00:41:22.760 --> 00:41:28.160
I don't think you'll do you're afraid I haven't the nerd no no it isn't that you

00:41:28.160 --> 00:41:28.700
haven't the

00:41:30.060 --> 00:41:32.680
You haven't the, uh, the, uh...

00:41:32.710 --> 00:41:35.220
Peggy, what's going on down there?

00:41:36.040 --> 00:41:37.220
Nothing much yet.

00:41:38.000 --> 00:41:40.220
You better come in. It's safer in here.

00:41:40.880 --> 00:41:42.740
I can take care of myself, all right.

00:41:43.400 --> 00:41:44.660
Oh, I mean Peggy.

00:41:48.240 --> 00:41:48.600
Tomorrow?

00:41:49.520 --> 00:41:53.000
Yes, that's all right, but not Sunday.

00:41:54.050 --> 00:41:56.100
Well, good night.

00:42:00.700 --> 00:42:02.120
Good night.

00:42:38.990 --> 00:42:43.520
everybody. Mr. Story is on his way up in the elevator now. He'll be right here.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.080
It's all right, Mr. Storey.

00:43:01.220 --> 00:43:02.060
Step right this way.

00:43:15.260 --> 00:43:17.060
We'll be ready in a moment, Mr. Storey.

00:43:18.190 --> 00:43:18.830
No rush.

00:43:19.700 --> 00:43:21.580
Oh, how do you feel, Mr. Storey?

00:43:22.340 --> 00:43:23.240
Weak but willing.

00:43:23.380 --> 00:43:24.320
He feels great.

00:43:27.000 --> 00:43:28.440
Right this way, Mr. Storey.

00:43:28.480 --> 00:43:28.780
Yes, sir.

00:43:30.380 --> 00:43:32.680
This is a simple little test of second hearing.

00:43:33.000 --> 00:43:34.720
You won't have any trouble passing it.

00:43:35.120 --> 00:43:36.260
You think not, huh?

00:43:37.070 --> 00:43:39.630
Are there any traces of insanity in your family, Mr. Story?

00:43:40.300 --> 00:43:41.400
Insanity in our family?

00:43:42.630 --> 00:43:43.630
No, I guess not.

00:43:43.900 --> 00:43:46.980
Just to prove it, my Uncle George, who thought he was Napoleon,

00:43:47.140 --> 00:43:48.820
tried to hang himself one day in the barn.

00:43:49.080 --> 00:43:52.560
Father, who had the silly idea that he was Santa Claus, rushed out to save him.

00:43:53.300 --> 00:43:55.000
He says to Uncle George, he says, I won't save you,

00:43:55.080 --> 00:43:57.240
but if I can find another rope, I'll get up there with you.

00:43:57.840 --> 00:43:59.080
So Mother handed him the rope.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:01.900
while Aunt Harriet stood on her head in the corner

00:44:01.900 --> 00:44:03.120
and laughed herself to death.

00:44:03.580 --> 00:44:07.020
But there's no trace of insanity in our family.

00:44:07.910 --> 00:44:08.450
Uh-huh.

00:44:09.280 --> 00:44:11.540
Oh, just put down playful relatives.

00:44:12.530 --> 00:44:14.450
All ready for that little eye and ear test.

00:44:14.800 --> 00:44:16.860
Miss Baker, will you please manipulate the card?

00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:17.650
Yes, Doctor.

00:44:20.840 --> 00:44:21.620
Can you read that?

00:44:24.400 --> 00:44:24.680
No.

00:44:27.330 --> 00:44:27.550
That?

00:44:30.030 --> 00:44:32.170
I'll bet it's something easy, like spatula.

00:44:32.550 --> 00:44:35.700
It's very easy. Can you read it now?

00:44:39.880 --> 00:44:45.990
Not yet, but it's an eight-letter word, beginning with X.

00:44:47.360 --> 00:44:48.340
It's a B, you fool.

00:44:48.800 --> 00:44:51.140
I know it's a B, but I'm no fool.

00:44:52.020 --> 00:44:52.720
Can you hear this, watch?

00:44:54.430 --> 00:44:55.050
What watch?

00:44:55.380 --> 00:44:56.420
Can you read it now?

00:44:57.780 --> 00:44:58.700
What's in it for me?

00:44:59.170 --> 00:44:59.630
Hear that?

00:45:01.630 --> 00:45:02.590
Did someone speak?

00:45:07.780 --> 00:45:08.380
You hear that?

00:45:09.100 --> 00:45:09.360
Yep.

00:45:10.380 --> 00:45:11.280
It's an Ingersoll.

00:45:18.830 --> 00:45:21.970
I've met a cop under the conjunctiva.

00:45:22.530 --> 00:45:23.630
Slightly traumatic.

00:45:24.900 --> 00:45:25.620
There, you see?

00:45:26.070 --> 00:45:27.170
I can't fly.

00:45:27.370 --> 00:45:28.110
Why, that's nothing.

00:45:28.270 --> 00:45:29.550
That comes from starchy foods.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.260
That's why I can't fly.

00:45:31.460 --> 00:45:32.880
Why, you don't know what starch is.

00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:34.000
Oh, yes, I do.

00:45:34.620 --> 00:45:36.500
Tell me three things containing starch.

00:45:36.700 --> 00:45:38.100
Oh, I know, all right.

00:45:38.260 --> 00:45:40.340
All right, name me three containing starch.

00:45:41.280 --> 00:45:43.290
A collar and two cuffs.

00:45:44.290 --> 00:45:45.950
Right this way, Mr. Storty, please.

00:45:48.820 --> 00:45:50.220
You're gonna fall down on us, are you?

00:45:50.460 --> 00:45:53.100
Ah, cherish the thought, my dear fellow.

00:45:53.240 --> 00:45:54.080
Cherish the thought.

00:45:54.410 --> 00:45:56.770
You know that I can't see two feet in front of me.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:01.420
Uh, now sit here, Mr. Story.

00:46:01.640 --> 00:46:03.180
We want to test your heart.

00:46:03.300 --> 00:46:04.020
Oh, no, you don't.

00:46:04.320 --> 00:46:05.340
Not my heart.

00:46:05.600 --> 00:46:06.660
It isn't working today.

00:46:07.360 --> 00:46:07.760
Working?

00:46:07.980 --> 00:46:10.400
No, say, sometimes, for weeks and weeks,

00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:11.820
my heart don't beat a stroke.

00:46:12.570 --> 00:46:14.050
Well, I'll look into that.

00:46:14.210 --> 00:46:14.910
Please sit down.

00:46:15.110 --> 00:46:16.690
Well, all right, but be careful.

00:46:16.870 --> 00:46:18.330
My heart is easily broken.

00:46:19.240 --> 00:46:21.590
Uh, Doctor, will you get the heartometer, please?

00:46:21.790 --> 00:46:22.610
Yes, just a moment, Doctor.

00:46:23.240 --> 00:46:24.980
First, I'll take a look at your tonsils.

00:46:25.160 --> 00:46:26.780
I see, just to start off.

00:46:29.080 --> 00:46:29.920
Open your mouth.

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:33.540
Just your mouth, Mr. Storey.

00:46:34.630 --> 00:46:35.350
That's better.

00:46:37.260 --> 00:46:38.460
This won't hurt you.

00:46:41.010 --> 00:46:44.310
Once more, please.

00:46:44.590 --> 00:46:46.250
A little more flamboyantly.

00:46:48.660 --> 00:46:52.960
What tonsils?

00:46:53.560 --> 00:46:56.020
Have you ever been advised to have your tonsils out?

00:46:56.640 --> 00:46:59.480
Well, you have to go for a try to check out one.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:02.280
Exactly. And you take cold easily?

00:47:02.900 --> 00:47:06.700
I thought so.

00:47:07.470 --> 00:47:09.770
Let me look a little wider now.

00:47:11.660 --> 00:47:11.900
Oh.

00:47:13.750 --> 00:47:14.870
Lungs congested.

00:47:16.230 --> 00:47:17.470
And Mr. Story.

00:47:18.720 --> 00:47:19.760
Fallen arches.

00:47:20.460 --> 00:47:22.000
Fallen arches, Mr. Story.

00:47:22.020 --> 00:47:22.940
Are you a coin arches?

00:47:23.080 --> 00:47:23.400
Yes.

00:47:24.830 --> 00:47:25.660
Beg pardon?

00:47:26.620 --> 00:47:27.520
Everything's ready, Doctor.

00:47:29.010 --> 00:47:29.350
All right.

00:47:31.110 --> 00:47:32.890
Ground it there, Doctor, please.

00:47:35.200 --> 00:47:36.440
What did I do with that spoon?

00:47:36.620 --> 00:47:38.760
I swallowed it.

00:47:39.720 --> 00:47:41.980
Well, never mind. We'll get another one later.

00:47:43.680 --> 00:47:45.220
Get a knife and fork, too.

00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:55.450
Mr. Story, this is a simple little device

00:47:55.450 --> 00:47:59.830
that permits us to listen to your heartbeats through this amplifier.

00:48:00.280 --> 00:48:04.220
I bet you a dollar I haven't even got a heart.

00:48:06.860 --> 00:48:08.120
Now, turn it on, please.

00:48:19.410 --> 00:48:24.110
Yes, and a little irregular.

00:48:32.170 --> 00:48:33.000
What's that noise?

00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:33.220
What's that noise?

00:48:33.860 --> 00:48:34.600
Robby Hart.

00:48:34.760 --> 00:48:35.360
How are you?

00:48:35.580 --> 00:48:37.580
Don't get excited, Mr. Story.

00:48:38.680 --> 00:48:43.360
This is the worst case of hyperstatic thrombosis I've seen in 20 years.

00:48:46.360 --> 00:48:48.080
That means that I'm sick, huh?

00:48:48.470 --> 00:48:48.830
Oh, no.

00:49:02.520 --> 00:49:05.930
He has a leaky heart. He's a very sick man.

00:49:06.520 --> 00:49:07.300
Shut it off, Doctor.

00:49:07.600 --> 00:49:09.640
Now, that's what I told you, see?

00:49:10.540 --> 00:49:12.840
All right, Mr. Storey. We'll attend to it.

00:49:12.920 --> 00:49:13.740
Come right along.

00:49:14.000 --> 00:49:14.540
Right over here.

00:49:14.950 --> 00:49:15.990
Right in, Mr. Storey.

00:49:17.120 --> 00:49:22.080
Now, Mr. Storey, we're going to give you the new stereoscopic gamma ray test.

00:49:22.660 --> 00:49:24.760
This will enable us to see right through you.

00:49:25.320 --> 00:49:26.200
How's the voltage, boys?

00:49:26.380 --> 00:49:27.800
It's pretty well up. 4,000 amps.

00:49:28.080 --> 00:49:28.720
I think it's five.

00:49:31.180 --> 00:49:32.960
Is there a doctor in the crowd?

00:49:35.750 --> 00:49:37.250
Are you naturally nervous?

00:49:38.160 --> 00:49:39.100
Naturally not.

00:49:39.360 --> 00:49:40.080
This will tell.

00:49:42.450 --> 00:49:43.210
Turn it on to yourself.

00:49:46.240 --> 00:49:47.380
Doctor, turn it on, please.

00:50:10.080 --> 00:50:10.700
How does it look?

00:50:11.670 --> 00:50:13.390
Not very good, Mr. Story.

00:50:15.280 --> 00:50:15.940
That's fine.

00:50:16.700 --> 00:50:19.480
I see an extraneous object in there.

00:50:20.680 --> 00:50:21.240
Extraneous?

00:50:22.480 --> 00:50:25.100
Maybe that's that harmonica I lost last summer.

00:50:30.800 --> 00:50:32.020
You're shaking on purpose.

00:50:32.720 --> 00:50:35.940
If you don't like the way I shake, get in here and try it yourself.

00:50:36.880 --> 00:50:39.270
Get out of here.

00:50:39.720 --> 00:50:40.900
I'm being barbecued.

00:50:41.060 --> 00:50:42.060
Doctor, shut it off, please.

00:50:44.860 --> 00:50:46.040
Right this way, Mr. Story.

00:50:46.280 --> 00:50:46.440
What?

00:50:46.680 --> 00:50:46.880
More?

00:50:48.130 --> 00:50:49.230
Step right up, Mr. Story.

00:50:49.430 --> 00:50:50.930
There's hardly a chance of getting hurt.

00:50:51.860 --> 00:50:52.980
Yes, you ought to like this one.

00:50:56.200 --> 00:50:59.640
We'll put the belt on, Mr. Story, so you won't go up on your head.

00:51:01.280 --> 00:51:04.110
You'll find my will under the barn.

00:51:05.090 --> 00:51:07.410
Go on. Show them what you've got in you, Robert.

00:51:07.940 --> 00:51:10.320
I showed them what I've got in me over there.

00:51:10.960 --> 00:51:12.080
All ready, Mr. Story.

00:51:12.340 --> 00:51:14.300
Remember, when the chair stops spinning,

00:51:14.600 --> 00:51:15.900
you should not be dizzy.

00:51:17.570 --> 00:51:19.350
I won't be. I'll be dead.

00:51:19.960 --> 00:51:21.640
Now, young lady, if you'll step back, please.

00:51:23.530 --> 00:51:24.690
All ready, go!

00:52:03.600 --> 00:52:17.380
Oh, Robert. There, you poor boy. You'll be all right.

00:52:17.810 --> 00:52:20.060
Don't pretend you're dizzy. Dizzy.

00:52:57.800 --> 00:52:58.160
Am I?

00:53:08.730 --> 00:53:09.830
You put it down like a feather.

00:53:09.930 --> 00:53:10.550
Didn't I tell you?

00:53:10.730 --> 00:53:13.130
Hey, listen everybody, I got a great joke.

00:53:13.470 --> 00:53:14.270
Reaver's a sucker.

00:53:14.470 --> 00:53:15.970
I just made a little bet with him.

00:53:16.360 --> 00:53:18.160
Zach, what did you use for money?

00:53:18.340 --> 00:53:19.910
Oh, this, this is good.

00:53:20.320 --> 00:53:23.760
I bet our interest in the hotel against 25,000

00:53:23.760 --> 00:53:25.660
that Story would win the race.

00:53:28.620 --> 00:53:29.440
Isn't that soft?

00:53:40.550 --> 00:53:43.870
Wait a minute, you mean to say that your all is at stake?

00:53:44.690 --> 00:53:45.150
Everything.

00:53:45.510 --> 00:53:46.490
Your all in all?

00:53:47.040 --> 00:53:47.500
Our all?

00:53:49.510 --> 00:53:50.990
I defy the doctors.

00:53:51.230 --> 00:53:56.530
No one will ever say that a story would let a girl lose her all in all, in all, in all.

00:53:57.400 --> 00:53:58.940
I fly Saturday.

00:54:01.660 --> 00:54:02.780
Prepare the parachute.

00:54:03.840 --> 00:54:04.460
You all right?

00:54:05.950 --> 00:54:08.280
I'm absolutely scow-roo-y.

00:54:08.940 --> 00:54:21.640
Well, then, you remember all I told you about taking off.

00:54:23.750 --> 00:54:24.090
Understand?

00:54:26.940 --> 00:54:27.280
Yes.

00:54:28.130 --> 00:54:29.970
And the minute you're off the ground just tap...

00:54:30.660 --> 00:54:32.200
and he'll take over the plane.

00:54:33.120 --> 00:54:34.200
Then I pull this.

00:54:34.380 --> 00:54:34.700
No.

00:54:35.240 --> 00:54:36.740
You don't need that with Ferguson.

00:54:37.060 --> 00:54:37.380
No?

00:54:38.210 --> 00:54:40.470
I count six and pull this.

00:54:40.590 --> 00:54:41.690
They're waiting for you.

00:54:41.830 --> 00:54:42.610
Ready to start.

00:54:43.280 --> 00:54:43.800
Already?

00:54:46.260 --> 00:54:46.640
Soon?

00:54:46.920 --> 00:54:47.340
Yeah.

00:54:48.020 --> 00:54:48.900
What's the matter?

00:54:49.480 --> 00:54:51.780
He's always a little bit nervous just before a flight.

00:54:52.140 --> 00:54:52.820
Oh, damn.

00:54:53.020 --> 00:54:55.400
I got something to fix up those old nerves.

00:54:55.760 --> 00:54:56.380
Come on, sir.

00:55:08.190 --> 00:55:09.130
Open the door.

00:55:09.860 --> 00:55:12.020
This is Ferguson, the planet of the Blue Star.

00:55:30.670 --> 00:55:32.920
He's holding us up, Ben, waiting around here all day.

00:55:33.330 --> 00:55:34.830
No, no, no, no, no.

00:55:35.090 --> 00:55:36.730
This is flying time, oh boy.

00:55:36.970 --> 00:55:37.870
Now, wait a minute, boys.

00:55:38.090 --> 00:55:38.910
I have to go up.

00:55:39.720 --> 00:55:41.620
Wonderful what a little tomato juice will do.

00:55:41.910 --> 00:55:43.310
What would he do behind a gallon?

00:55:44.220 --> 00:55:45.600
I'd drink it, boys, drink it.

00:55:45.600 --> 00:55:46.920
Hurry up, let's your Benton play.

00:55:47.080 --> 00:55:48.660
Benton, Benton, where is that guy?

00:55:48.760 --> 00:55:50.120
Let me at him, let me at him.

00:55:50.140 --> 00:55:50.840
Take it easy, take it easy.

00:55:50.840 --> 00:55:52.580
Don't hold, wait a minute, don't hold me.

00:55:52.980 --> 00:55:55.160
Bring on your Benton, bring on your balloons.

00:55:55.680 --> 00:55:57.430
Give me altitude, altitude.

00:56:05.270 --> 00:56:10.220
All right, old boy.

00:56:11.570 --> 00:56:12.430
Freeman? Yes?

00:56:12.920 --> 00:56:14.120
Are the conditions understood?

00:56:14.460 --> 00:56:14.740
Yes.

00:56:15.140 --> 00:56:17.040
The one that stays in the air the longer wins.

00:56:17.280 --> 00:56:18.400
And I know, Mr. Story.

00:56:19.360 --> 00:56:20.800
Oh, here comes Story now.

00:56:22.430 --> 00:56:23.090
Good luck to you, friend.

00:56:23.750 --> 00:56:25.030
Hope you'll run a close second.

00:56:25.310 --> 00:56:26.890
I see you've got your parachute with you.

00:56:27.080 --> 00:56:28.160
Don't worry about me.

00:56:28.340 --> 00:56:29.180
Worry about yourself.

00:56:30.030 --> 00:56:31.830
And don't get in my way, I'm telling you.

00:56:32.010 --> 00:56:35.060
Don't get in my way, or I'll slam you through a cloud.

00:56:35.360 --> 00:56:36.200
Come on, Mr. Story.

00:56:36.440 --> 00:56:37.120
Well, all right.

00:56:37.500 --> 00:56:38.860
Don't worry about anything, Mr. Howard.

00:56:39.000 --> 00:56:40.280
Everything is going to be all right.

00:56:40.420 --> 00:56:41.520
I know it will.

00:56:49.950 --> 00:56:50.730
Wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:56:50.850 --> 00:56:51.710
Don't rush me.

00:56:52.220 --> 00:56:53.440
Nip me, boy, nip me.

00:56:53.540 --> 00:56:54.460
It's all gone.

00:56:54.800 --> 00:56:55.100
What?

00:56:55.320 --> 00:56:55.760
Come on.

00:56:55.920 --> 00:56:56.480
Go on, get him.

00:56:57.030 --> 00:56:58.540
Hey, can I count on him?

00:56:58.680 --> 00:56:59.820
Sure, just tap him on the shoulder.

00:57:07.780 --> 00:57:20.780
Okay, got it.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:30.260
See you next time.

00:59:45.610 --> 00:59:47.090
You're a person with a smart fella.

00:59:47.230 --> 00:59:48.230
Look in here.

00:59:48.550 --> 00:59:48.990
Yes, sir.

00:59:49.090 --> 00:59:49.270
What?

00:59:50.500 --> 00:59:51.200
Coming off here.

00:59:51.530 --> 00:59:53.350
Who locked me in the closet inside the hangar?

00:59:53.500 --> 00:59:54.220
Locked you!

00:59:55.780 --> 00:59:56.040
Plane!

01:00:00.700 --> 01:00:02.200
She picked a fine time for it.

01:00:02.620 --> 01:00:05.620
Hey, this will give Peggy the biggest kick.

01:00:06.620 --> 01:00:07.280
Isn't that great?

01:00:07.644 --> 01:00:09.384
Give Peggy the biggest kick there is.

01:02:06.310 --> 01:02:09.800
Why? Why, I agreed to an air raid, not a suicide pack.

01:02:10.020 --> 01:02:11.940
There isn't room enough up there for both of us.

01:02:12.100 --> 01:02:13.180
That fellow's a maniac.

01:02:15.100 --> 01:02:16.600
Well, I'll get you one, Howard.

01:02:17.010 --> 01:02:18.070
Thanks to Benton.

01:02:18.130 --> 01:02:19.830
Thanks to Benton. I don't care who won.

01:02:19.950 --> 01:02:20.770
I'm glad I'm alive.

01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:22.460
Well, you understand what the weight you want?

01:02:22.640 --> 01:02:23.240
The idea was...

01:02:23.240 --> 01:02:24.780
No! There's a story now!

01:02:45.860 --> 01:02:47.120
Why don't he come down?

01:02:47.610 --> 01:02:48.270
He'll be down.

01:02:48.390 --> 01:02:49.580
Won't be long now.

01:02:49.820 --> 01:02:51.840
What are you so nervous about?

01:02:52.640 --> 01:02:54.120
There's been a terrible mistake, Mr. Howard.

01:02:54.220 --> 01:02:54.480
That's all.

01:02:54.680 --> 01:02:56.340
That isn't Robert's story up there.

01:02:56.500 --> 01:02:57.550
Who is it then?

01:02:58.180 --> 01:02:58.580
Lindbergh?

01:02:58.640 --> 01:02:58.880
No.

01:02:59.220 --> 01:02:59.720
The newspaper.

01:03:01.360 --> 01:03:02.860
What are you talking about?

01:03:04.280 --> 01:03:07.020
Well, Mr. Howard, you see, the girls

01:03:07.020 --> 01:03:08.560
were so set on winning the race, we

01:03:08.930 --> 01:03:10.090
didn't want to disappoint them.

01:03:10.170 --> 01:03:12.190
I'm madly in love with Ruth.

01:03:12.480 --> 01:03:13.680
I'm crazy about her.

01:03:14.140 --> 01:03:14.960
I've lost my mind.

01:03:16.080 --> 01:03:21.020
Never mind that. You mean to tell me that guy Smith up there is only an amateur pilot?

01:03:21.280 --> 01:03:24.080
He's no pilot. He's never been in a plane before in his life.

01:03:24.240 --> 01:03:24.520
What?

01:05:35.470 --> 01:05:36.770
deserves a nice girl.

01:05:37.010 --> 01:05:38.260
Do you want...

01:05:39.240 --> 01:05:41.740
I'm just crazy about you, Peggy, but...

01:05:42.340 --> 01:05:44.960
But I can't take a penny...

01:05:45.060 --> 01:05:45.840
Have you liked that?

01:05:45.960 --> 01:05:47.380
Well, yes or no.

01:05:47.910 --> 01:05:49.500
Ha, Peggy.

01:05:50.740 --> 01:05:51.340
I'm yours.
